<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Government of National Unity</h1><p class="st-meta">1944 CE – 1945 CE · capital Budapest</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Arrow Cross regime of Ferenc Szálasi, installed by Germany in October 1944, which brought terror to Budapest in the final months of the war.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>On 15 October 1944 Regent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/miklos-horthy">Miklós Horthy</a> announced that the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-hungary-1920-1946">Kingdom of Hungary</a> (1920-1946) was seeking an armistice with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> kidnapped his son and forced Horthy to abdicate in favour of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferenc-szalasi">Ferenc Szálasi</a>, leader of the fascist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arrow-cross-party">Arrow Cross Party</a>, who formed a Government of National Unity and took the title Leader of the Nation.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The regime continued the war on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany's</a> side, mobilising every remaining resource. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arrow-cross-party">Arrow Cross</a> militias murdered thousands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/budapest">Budapest</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a>, many shot into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a>, and tens of thousands were sent on death marches towards <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>, while diplomats such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raoul-wallenberg">Raoul Wallenberg</a> issued protective papers. A rival provisional government was formed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/debrecen">Debrecen</a> under Soviet protection in December 1944.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The Soviet siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/budapest">Budapest</a> ended in February 1945, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferenc-szalasi">Szálasi</a>'s government retreated west before collapsing in April 1945. Szálasi was captured by American troops, handed over to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>, and tried and executed in Budapest in 1946.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/government-of-national-unity.jpg" alt="Government of National Unity" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Zscout370, colour correction: R-41, current version: Thommy · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Hungary_(1915-1918,_1919-1946).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1944 CE – 1945 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Budapest</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ferenc Szálasi</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic and Protestant Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Hungarian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/hungary">Hungary</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Arrow Cross Hungary, Szálasi government</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1944&amp;focus=government-of-national-unity" aria-label="Government of National Unity on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5125 512 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Government of National Unity lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5445 768L5445 768M5445 768L5300 622M5445 768L5820 533"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5445 768h0M5300 622h0M5820 533h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5445 768h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5445 768h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Budapest. <a href="/atlas?year=1944&amp;focus=government-of-national-unity">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
